{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 6,
      "name": "Ice Slide",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "A slide is a shaped track (slope, turns, lip), and its feel depends on hand-tuned angles and speeds. A random track could easily make a turn you can't steer through, so each variant is built and tested by hand.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "\"ice\" look and the ice = true flag (no friction) from Ice Gauntlet",
          "spinning bar on a post (spin motion) for sweepers",
          "flat slabs, so holes are just gaps between ice slabs",
          "red see-through hazard look and the fall-back-to-start rule",
          "step and gap tests (GAP_MAX 6, RISE_MAX 3.5 at walking speed)",
          "Ice Gauntlet section today: flat ice slab with spinning sweeper bars (BUILD.IceGauntlet)"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Ramps: a tilted slab (a pitch angle on a part), the same piece Rolling Blobs (14) plans; fall height measured from the bottom of the slope",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Slide controller on the client: on ice you keep your speed, the slope pulls you downhill, and walking only steers (you can't stop). A speed cap keeps it fair. Friction 0 alone does not make a default character slide much. Must not fight Speed Strip's (16) boost controller if both sit in one course",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Turned parts (a yaw field), the same one Speed Strip (16) plans, plus a bank (roll) angle, so curves and hairpins are short turned and tilted wedge segments",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Soft side rails (low padded walls) that stop you sliding off; they do not push",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Brake goo: a dripping green sticky patch on the ice that brings the slide to a stop (the only place you can stand still); same green goo look as Sticky Walls (22)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Hazard touch = back to the start pad, shared with Crusher Alley (1) and every hazard idea",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Test that a slide-jump clears its gap at the capped slide speed (the walking GAP_MAX does not apply to the end jump)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Frost sparkles on the ice and a skid sound while you slide",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "Glossy pale-blue ice with frost sparkles and a skid sound the moment you step on it; the track always tilts down, so you know you will keep moving. Red see-through goo patches and dark holes in the ice show where not to steer. Dripping green goo on the ice is the one place you can stop.",
